**Faculty position in Arctic defence and security**

**Advertiser:** École Supérieure d’Etudes Internationales, Université Laval

**Field(s) of specialization:** 
International Finance/Macro
- International Trade
- Law and Economics
- Political Economy

**Position type(s):**
Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Full Professor

**Location of job:**
Pavillon Charles-De Koninck, 1030, avenue des Sciences-Humaines,, Quebec City, Quebec, G1V 0A6, Canada

**Degree required:**
Doctorate

**Job start date:**
2027-06-01

**Job duration:**
Continuing/permanent

**Application deadline:** 30 Oct 2026 midnight [UTC](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coordinated_Universal_Time)
(accepting applications)

**Posting end date:** 30 Oct 2026

**Ad text:**

The Graduate School of International Studies (École supérieure d’études internationales – ESEI) at Université Laval, located in Quebec City (Canada), is a centre of excellence in multidisciplinary research and teaching on international affaires. ESEI is currently seeking applications for a faculty position on Arctic defence and security.

The competition is open to applicants from all disciplines relevant to the study of defence and security dynamics in the Arctic. Applications from scholars in economics, law, geography, history, management, political science, and other relevant disciplines are particularly encouraged.

The successful candidate will hold the Desgagnés Chair in Arctic Defence and Security and will have access to a research budget of more than $200,000 per year for five years.

The Chair’s mandate is to conduct leading-edge interdisciplinary research. In particular, it seeks to examine transformations in the Arctic strategic environment in a context marked by the return of great-power rivalry and by rapidly evolving economic, legal, geographic, and political realities in the region.

By bringing academic expertise to strategic issues of primary importance to Canada, the Chair seeks to contribute actively to national debates on defence and security.

Research conducted through the Chair may address, among other topics:

* The economic and geoeconomic dimensions of competition in the Arctic;
* The costs, choices, and trade-offs associated with defence and security policies in the region;
* The legal frameworks and governance issues that shape activities in the Arctic, particularly in a region where different and overlapping areas of state jurisdiction coexist;
* The historical and territorial transformations of the region and their implications for contemporary security issues;
* Transformations in the strategic environment and power relations in the Arctic;
* The resilience and security of critical northern infrastructure, particularly land and maritime transportation infrastructure;
* Maritime security and the evolution of commercial shipping;
* The development and transportation of natural resources and their strategic implications.

A research advisor will support the Chairholder in developing, planning, and submitting research grant applications, while also helping to maximize the Chair’s outreach and engagement activities. Funding will also be available to offer doctoral scholarships associated with the Chair.

The successful candidate will join the Graduate School of International Studies as a regular faculty member starting June 1, 2027, and no later than September 1, 2027. Hiring may be at any academic rank in accordance with the Collective Agreement between Laval University and the Syndicat des professeurs et des professeures de l’Université Laval (SPUL).

Duties include:

* Teaching at the graduate level;
* Supervising master’s essays, dissertations and doctoral theses;
* Conducting research and publishing on Arctic defence and security;
* Participating in School-related pedagogical and administrative activities;
* Being involved in any other activity provided for in the Université Laval-SPUL collective agreement;
* Selection criteria:
* Ability to teach in French within three years of appointment.
* Hold a PhD in a field relevant to Arctic defence and security;
* Applications from doctoral candidates nearing completion of their PhD will be considered, provided that a letter from the department chair confirms the expected date of submission or defense;
* Demonstrate strong commitment to pluri-/interdisciplinarity, whether through academic background, research program, teaching experience, or collaborative projects;
* An excellent research record, with publications in top peer-reviewed journals in the candidate’s field, or strong potential to develop such a record for early-career applicants;
* University-level teaching experience;
* A proven track record of securing research funding from recognized granting agencies, or strong potential to obtain such funding in the near future;
* Ability to teach a graduate-level methodology course.
* Proven integration into national and international research networks is considered an asset.
* Employment conditions:
* Regular full-time position;
* Salary based on recognized experience with benefits in accordance with the Université Laval-SPUL collective agreement (available in French only) <https://www.rh.ulaval.ca/personnel-enseignant-et-derecherche/professeurs/conventions-collectives>
* Applications:
* Application deadline: October 30, 2026
* Starting date: June 1, 2027 (no later than September 1, 2027).

The application file must include:

1. A cover letter demonstrating the candidate’s commitment to pluri/interdisciplinarity and international studies;
2. A curriculum vitae;
3. A document of no more than two pages outlining a proposed five-year research chair program;
4. A sample publication.

Valuing equity, diversity, and excellence, Université Laval is firmly committed to providing all its staff with a work and living environment characterized by an inclusive culture. For Université Laval, diversity is a source of strength, and we encourage qualified individuals of all origins, genders, sexual orientations, gender identities or expressions, as well as individuals with disabilities, to apply.

Université Laval also adheres to an employment equity program for women, members of visible or ethnic minorities, Indigenous peoples, and individuals with disabilities. To this end, all applicants will be invited to complete a confidential self-identification form upon submission of their application.

All applications will be processed confidentially.

Applications must be sent to:

Jonathan Paquin  
Director  
Graduate School of International Studies  
Université Laval  
recrutement.esei@ulaval.ca

**Analyst Intern - Generalist / Stage - Analyste - Généraliste - Paris 2027 Start**

**Advertiser:** Analysis Group

**Field(s) of specialization:** 
Econometrics

**Position type(s):**
Consultant

**Location of job:**
9 Rue d'Argenson, Paris, 75008, France

**Degree required:**
Masters

**Job start date:**
Flexible

**Job duration:**
6 months

**Application deadline:** 12 Mar 2027 midnight [UTC](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coordinated_Universal_Time)
(accepting applications)

**Posting end date:** 12 Mar 2027

**Ad text:**

Overview
--------

Analysis Group is one of the largest international economics consulting firms, with more than 1,500 professionals across 15 offices in North America, Europe, and Asia. Since 1981, we have provided expertise in economics, finance, health care analytics, and strategy to top law firms, Fortune Global 500 companies, and government agencies worldwide. Our internal experts, together with our network of affiliated experts from academia, industry, and government, offer our clients exceptional breadth and depth of expertise.

Staff in the Paris office specialize in antitrust, competition, strategy, and public policy analysis. They manage cases in a wide range of sectors (technology companies, pharmaceuticals, insurance, transport, public services, media, mass retail, energy, etc.) relating to:

* **Commercial disputes** (development of theoretical economic reasoning on the potential impact of anti-competitive practices such as cartels, vertical restraints and abuse of dominant position, measurement of these practices on prices, estimation of damages due to an injured party);
* **Economic assessment of mergers and acquisitions** (assessment of effects on competition, data analysis, calculation of market shares and market studies as part of merger notification activities before the French Competition Authority or the European Commission);
* **Government reforms** (economic evaluation of regulations and the effectiveness of public aid through the development of before-and-after, double-difference econometric models, etc.);
* **Corporate strategy** (econometric analysis of demand, pricing strategy, growth strategies through analysis of market dynamics, innovation strategies, identification of growth markets).

Analysis Group fosters a work environment that is centered on delivering high quality work through teamwork and collaboration, best-in-class learning programs, and a culture of transparency, trust and respect.

In 2022, Analysis Group was ranked among the world leaders in competition economics by the Global Competition Review (GCR) and is among the 10 consulting firms worldwide with the best working conditions in 2023 according to Vault.

**Analyst Intern Position:**

This is a position for master’s 2 students (or gap year students) working towards a degree in economics, econometrics, or statistics, with relevant professional or research experience. Students with no previous experience are also welcome to apply if they can demonstrate an excellent academic record and a strong motivation for the proposed assignments.

Within an inclusive and collaborative environment, Analyst Interns may have the opportunity to be involved on multiple projects at a time across various practice areas and industries. Depending on the candidate’s profile and skills, the assignments and responsibilities may include:

* Analyzing economic and financial data using algorithms and statistical programming in R and Stata (econometric estimation of models, machine learning, etc.);
* Creating insightful figures for exploratory purposes and to summarize information;
* Developing theoretical economic reasoning based on research findings (in antitrust and competition policy);
* Examining market and industry behavior through targeted research;
* Reviewing and summarizing reports and client documents;
* Writing reports and memos to present the quantitative and theoretical analyses carried out.

Analysis Group fosters an academically oriented work environment, with an emphasis on teamwork (including with our other international offices) and collaboration across diverse areas of expertise. On arrival, Analyst Interns are given a series of training courses to help them get up to speed quickly and integrate more easily into the team. Specifically, we seek candidates with:

* A strong interest in statistical programming and applying quantitative methods to real world research problems;
* A strong interest in economics, particularly competition economics and industrial organization;
* An excellent academic record;
* Strong interpersonal and communication skills, inclusive and growth-oriented mindset;
* Interest in teamwork and collaborative problem solving;
* Willingness to learn new skills and share knowledge with other team members;
* Excellent command of English and/or French.

While Analysis Group sponsors work authorization for full-time positions, we do not offer sponsorship for internships. Accordingly, candidates must already be lawfully authorized to work in the EU for Analysis Group for the duration of the internship.

Analysis Group embraces diversity and equal opportunity in a deep and meaningful way. We are committed to building teams that represent a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. The more inclusive we are, the better our work will be. We encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply.

**How to Apply:**

When submitting your CV, please include a cover letter and your bachelor’s and master’s transcripts (temporary documents accepted for those whose studies are in progress). **You will also need to attach a writing sample with your application,** which can take the form of a thesis, essay, article, or group project writing sample you have completed.

**Other Information:**

*Nothing in this Job Description restricts Analysis Group SAS’s right to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this position at any time.*

