Analyst Intern - Corporate Finance / Stage - Analyste - Finance d'Entreprise - Paris (2027 Start Date)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Overview
--------

Analysis Group is one of the largest international economics consulting firms, with more than 1,500 professionals across 15 offices in North America, Europe, and Asia. Since 1981, we have provided expertise in economics, finance, health care analytics, and strategy to top law firms, Fortune Global 500 companies, and government agencies worldwide. Our internal experts, together with our network of affiliated experts from academia, industry, and government, offer our clients exceptional breadth and depth of expertise.

Since 2026, Ricol Lasteyrie has joined Analysis Group, combining both firms’ economic, financial, non-financial, and strategic consulting expertise to offer an integrated, multidisciplinary approach to addressing complex strategic, financial, and regulatory challenges across Europe and globally.

Staff in the Paris office specialize in corporate finance, antitrust, competition, strategy, and public policy analysis. They manage cases in a wide range of sectors (technology companies, pharmaceuticals, insurance, transport, public services, media, mass retail, energy, etc.). The Corporate Finance practice provides expertise across four core areas:

* **Strategic advisory** (definition, assessment, and implementation of strategic priorities, supported by rigorous economic and financial analysis);
* **M and A advisory** (support throughout all stages of financing and M and A transactions, combining financial, strategic, and organizational expertise);
* **Business and enterprise valuation** (valuation of businesses, assets, and liabilities across a broad range of strategic and regulatory contexts);
* **Special situations** (support in situations involving financial distress, restructuring, or litigation, drawing on deep technical expertise and experience in complex situations).

Staff in the Paris office specialize in antitrust, competition, strategy, and public policy analysis. They manage cases in a wide range of sectors (technology companies, pharmaceuticals, insurance, transport, public services, media, mass retail, energy, etc.) relating to:

* **Commercial disputes** (development of theoretical economic reasoning on the potential impact of anti-competitive practices such as cartels, vertical restraints and abuse of dominant position, measurement of these practices on prices, estimation of damages due to an injured party);
* **Economic assessment of mergers and acquisitions** (assessment of effects on competition, data analysis, calculation of market shares and market studies as part of merger notification activities before the French Competition Authority or the European Commission);
* **Government reforms** (economic evaluation of regulations and the effectiveness of public aid through the development of before-and-after, double-difference econometric models, etc.);
* **Corporate strategy** (econometric analysis of demand, pricing strategy, growth strategies through analysis of market dynamics, innovation strategies, identification of growth markets).

Analysis Group fosters a work environment that is centered on delivering high quality work through teamwork and collaboration, best-in-class learning programs, and a culture of transparency, trust and respect.

In 2022, Analysis Group was ranked among the world leaders in competition economics by the Global Competition Review (GCR) and is among the 10 consulting firms worldwide with the best working conditions in 2023 according to Vault.

**Analyst Intern Position:**

This is a position for master’s 2 students (or gap year students) at a leading business school, engineering school, or university, specializing in corporate finance with prior experience in M and A, Private Equity, Transaction Services, or equivalent.

Students with no previous experience are also welcome to apply if they can demonstrate an excellent academic record and a strong motivation for the proposed assignments.

Within an inclusive and collaborative environment, Analyst Interns may have the opportunity to be involved on multiple projects at a time across various practice areas and industries. Depending on the candidate’s profile and skills, the assignments and responsibilities may include:

* Strategic and financial assessment (industry analysis and performance analysis);
* Critical review of business plans;
* Company valuation (DCF, trading and transaction comparables, etc.);
* Preparation of presentations (valuation reports, pitch decks, client materials);
* Financial assessment of damages in the context of litigation.

Analysis Group fosters an academically oriented work environment, with an emphasis on teamwork (including with our other international offices) and collaboration across diverse areas of expertise. On arrival, Analyst Interns are given a series of training courses to help them get up to speed quickly and integrate more easily into the team. Specifically, we seek candidates with:

* A strong interest in corporate finance, valuation, financial modelling, and motivation to tackle complex financial problems and support clients on high-impact strategic decisions;
* Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to synthesize complex information;
* A solid understanding of accounting and financial statements;
* An excellent academic record;
* Strong interpersonal and communication skills, inclusive and growth-oriented mindset;
* Interest in teamwork and collaborative problem solving;
* Willingness to learn new skills and share knowledge with other team members;
* Proficient in Microsoft Office tools (Excel, Word, PowerPoint);
* Excellent command of English and French.

While Analysis Group sponsors work authorization for full-time positions, we do not offer sponsorship for internships. Accordingly, candidates must already be lawfully authorized to work in the EU for Analysis Group for the duration of the internship.

Analysis Group embraces diversity and equal opportunity in a deep and meaningful way. We are committed to building teams that represent a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. The more inclusive we are, the better our work will be. We encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply.

**How to Apply:**

When submitting your CV, please include a cover letter and your bachelor’s and master’s transcripts (temporary documents accepted for those whose studies are in progress).

**Other Information:**

*Nothing in this Job Description restricts Analysis Group SAS’s right to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this position at any time.*

