**Ad text:**

Analyst Intern - Health Care (HEOR, Epidemiology and Market Access) / Stage - Analyste - Économie de la santé et épidémiologie - Paris (2027 Start Date)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Overview

**About Analysis Group's HEOR Practice:**

Analysis Group is one of the largest economic consulting firms, with more than 1,500 professionals in 15 offices across North America, Europe, and Asia. Our specialists in health economics and epidemiology apply their analytical expertise to research projects in health economics and outcomes research (HEOR), clinical and pharmaceutical research, and health policy. Our in-house experts, in collaboration with our network of affiliated experts from academia, industry and government, offer our clients a range of cutting-edge multidisciplinary skills, particularly in health economics, biostatistics, econometrics, statistics, epidemiology and psychometrics.

The research we conduct has a significant impact on medical knowledge and patients’ lives. For example, we contributed to research on the Covid-19 vaccine in partnership with Pfizer and our teams have helped bring individually tailored, precision medical treatments to market. Our work also regularly results in high-impact publications in internationally recognized scientific journals.

**About the Analyst Intern Position:**

Analyst Interns often re-join the firm to start their career as full-time employees. Full-time Analysts with bachelor’s degrees go on to top graduate programs; some return as Associates after graduate school. Many Analysts with advanced degrees progress to the Associate level.

As an Analyst Intern, you have the opportunity to work on complex business problems within a collaborative environment. Analyst Interns can expect to work on multiple projects at a time with the opportunity to use different methods and work on different disease areas. Responsibilities and work experiences may include but are not limited to the following:

* Analyze health care data using statistical and analytical tools (e.g., econometric model estimation, survival analysis, machine learning) using R, SAS, Stata, Python, VBA and others;
* Analyzing health care data from a variety of sources including administrative claims data, clinical trial data, registries, medical chart data, and patient survey data;
* Conducting a range of health economics analyses such as treatment pattern and outcomes, comparative effectiveness, cost-effectiveness, and budget impact;
* Creating dynamic visualizations to rapidly explore data and models;
* Participating in meetings with medical experts, clients, and case team members;
* Assisting in the preparation of study reports, manuscripts for publication in peer-reviewed journals, abstracts and posters for presentation to scientific conferences, and other client deliverables.

We seek candidates who are pursuing a master’s degree, graduating in winter 2027 or spring/summer 2028, and have:

* A degree in biostatistics, computer science, data science, economics, epidemiology, health economics, health policy, mathematics, physics, psychometrics, public health, statistics, or related subjects;
* Passion for data analytics and healthcare research;
* Demonstrated analytical, quantitative, and organizational skills;
* Experience or a strong interest in statistical programming and data analysis;
* Strong interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills;
* An excellent academic record;
* Familiarity with AI tools;
* Effectively worked independently and within a team;
* Excellent attention to detail;
* A desire to continuously learn and develop professionally;
* Excellent command of English and French.

While Analysis Group sponsors work authorization for full-time positions, we do not offer sponsorship for internships. Accordingly, candidates must already be lawfully authorized to work in the EU for Analysis Group for the duration of the internship.

Analysis Group embraces diversity and equal opportunity in a deep and meaningful way. We are committed to building teams that represent a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. The more inclusive we are, the better our work will be. We encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply.

To learn more about Analysis Group, please check out our interactive brochure: [AG Recruiting Brochure (analysisgroupfiles.com)](https://analysisgroupfiles.com/recruiting/).

**How to Apply:**

When submitting your CV, please include a cover letter and your bachelor’s and master’s transcripts (temporary documents accepted for those whose studies are in progress).

